[% set COMPONENTS_AND_OWNERSHIP -%]
| Component | Location | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| Library crate | `src` | Owns production behavior and its public API |
| Test suite | `tests` | Protects public contracts and behavior |
[%- endset %]

[% set DEPENDENCY_DIRECTION -%]
Tests may depend on the public crate. Production code must not depend on tests, generated output, or developer tooling.
[%- endset %]

[% set RUNTIME_DATA_FLOW -%]
No multi-component runtime flow exists in the initial scaffold.
[%- endset %]

[% set DIRECTORY_TREE -%]
```text
src/
└── lib.rs
tests/
└── smoke.rs
```
[%- endset %]

[% set RUNTIME_CONSTRAINTS -%]
The Rust 1.97.1 toolchain is required. The initial crate defines no network, storage, concurrency, latency, or deployment contract.
[%- endset %]

[% set NAMING_CONVENTIONS -%]
Crates use `kebab-case`; modules, functions, methods, and variables use `snake_case`; types and traits use `PascalCase`; constants use `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`; test names describe behavior in `snake_case`.
[%- endset %]

[% set TECHNOLOGY_STANDARDS -%]
### Rust

- Use the Rust 1.97.1 toolchain and edition 2024.
- Keep rustfmt and Clippy clean with warnings denied.
- Deny missing public documentation and broken intra-doc links in native Cargo lint tables.
- Use idiomatic rustdoc (`//!` and `///`) for public APIs and relevant Errors, Panics, Safety, and examples sections.
- Keep unsafe code forbidden unless an approved architecture decision requires it.
- Prefer explicit ownership, checked operations, and narrow public APIs.
- Add dependencies only for concrete requirements.
[%- endset %]

[% set COVERAGE_REQUIREMENTS -%]
Coverage is enforced through `cargo llvm-cov` with line and region thresholds
at [[ coverage_target ]]%. The `just coverage` command produces a terminal
report with missed lines.
[%- endset %]

[% set TEST_LAYOUT -%]
The base scaffold contains one public crate-linkage test in `tests/smoke.rs`. Add other test levels only for real responsibilities.
[%- endset %]

[% set TECHNOLOGY_TESTING_STANDARDS -%]
### Rust testing

Use Cargo unit, integration, and documentation tests. Keep tests deterministic and protect public behavior rather than implementation details.
[%- endset %]

[% set TOOLCHAIN -%]
| Concern | Standard tool | Gate |
|---|---|---|
| Toolchain and dependencies | rustup and Cargo | Rust 1.97.1 and committed `Cargo.lock` |
| Formatting | rustfmt | No formatting differences |
| Linting | Clippy | Zero warnings |
| Dependency hygiene | cargo-shear | No unused dependencies |
| Supply chain | cargo-deny | No unapproved advisories, licenses, bans, or sources |
| Documentation | cargo doc | No broken intra-doc links or missing public docs |
| Testing and coverage | Cargo and cargo-llvm-cov | All tests pass; [[ coverage_target ]]% line and region coverage |
| Secret scanning | Gitleaks | No verified secrets |
| GitHub Actions security | zizmor | No unapproved findings |
[%- endset %]

[% set QUALITY_GATES -%]
| Gate | Required result |
|---|---|
| rustfmt | No formatting differences |
| Clippy | Zero warnings across workspace all-targets all-features |
| cargo-shear | No unused dependencies |
| cargo test | All target and documentation tests pass |
| cargo doc | No denied missing public docs or broken links |
| cargo llvm-cov | [[ coverage_target ]]% line and region coverage |
| cargo deny | No unapproved advisories, licenses, bans, or sources |
| Gitleaks | No verified secrets |
| zizmor | No unapproved GitHub Actions findings |
[%- endset %]

[% set SETUP_COMMANDS -%]
cargo install --locked --version 0.8.7 cargo-llvm-cov
cargo install --locked --version 0.20.2 cargo-deny
cargo install --locked --version 1.13.3 cargo-shear
pre-commit install --install-hooks
[%- endset %]

[% set VERIFY_COMMANDS -%]
cargo fmt --all --check
cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings
cargo shear --deny-warnings
cargo test --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked
cargo test --workspace --doc --all-features --locked
cargo doc --workspace --all-features --no-deps --locked
cargo llvm-cov --workspace --all-features --all-targets --locked --fail-under-lines [[ coverage_target ]] --fail-under-regions [[ coverage_target ]] --show-missing-lines
cargo deny --locked check
gitleaks git --redact --no-banner
zizmor --pedantic .
[%- endset %]

[% set DEVSECOPS_PROFILE -%]
cargo-deny enforces advisory, license, ban, and source policies. cargo-shear
detects unused dependencies. Gitleaks scans repository history and zizmor
analyzes GitHub Actions.
[%- endset %]
